  "h1": "Subsidized vs Unsubsidized Student Loans Compared",
  "introText": "A Direct Subsidized Loan is the better choice of the two whenever you qualify for one. The government does not charge interest on the subsidized loan while you are enrolled at least half-time, during your grace period, or during deferment. A Direct Unsubsidized Loan builds interest from the date of your first disbursement, and you owe all of it. Accept the subsidized amount first and borrow unsubsidized only to cover what is left. At The Modern Wallet, we compare subsidized vs unsubsidized student loans by tracking who pays the interest at each stage, then running the federal borrowing limits as plain arithmetic so you can see how much of each loan is available.",
